🩺 SAATHI: IoT-Based Smart Health Monitor & Fall Detection System
ESP32ArduinoTelegramJSONBin

SAATHI (meaning Companion or Partner in Hindi) is a smart, wearable/desktop IoT-enabled health monitoring and emergency response system built on the ESP32. It tracks critical patient vitals in real time, monitors environmental/body temperature, detects accidental falls, manages medication schedules, and provides immediate emergency SOS capabilities.

SAATHI ensures continuous safety by keeping caregivers updated via automated Telegram alerts and logging real-time telemetry to a cloud dashboard through JSONBin.

📌 Features
1. Vitals Monitoring
MAX30102/MAX30105 Sensor: Tracks real-time Heart Rate (BPM) and Oxygen Saturation (SpO2).
Maxim Algorithm Integration: Computes high-accuracy heart rate and SpO2 using standard buffer processing.
Signal Quality & Finger Detection: Analyzes I2C signal quality (Excellent/Good/Fair/Poor). Automatically detects when a user's finger is removed and issues a Telegram notification if the sensor remains detached for over 60 seconds.
2. Intelligent Fall Detection & Safety Countdown
MPU6050 Accelerometer: Monitors body movement dynamics.
Double-Threshold Detection: Triggers on a free-fall drop (FREEFALL_THRESHOLD), followed by a high-G impact (IMPACT_THRESHOLD) within a 600ms window.
10-Second Cancel Window: Upon impact, SAATHI starts a visual 10-second countdown on the LCD and sounds a buzzer. The user can press the SOS/Cancel button to abort false alarms.
Confirmed Alerts: If the countdown expires without intervention, the system rings a distinct siren, transmits the coordinate-based Google Maps location to caregivers via Telegram, and flags a critical fall on the cloud web dashboard.
3. Patient Vitals Analytics & Smarter Alerts
Health Score Algorithm (0–100): Automatically computes an overall health score based on deviations in heart rate, oxygen levels, and temperature.
Abnormality Persistence (Anti-False Triggering): Alerts are triggered only if abnormal parameters (BPM > 120, SpO2 < 94%, Temp > 38°C) persist for 3 consecutive readings, avoiding panic over single outlier readings.
Trend Analysis: Maintains a sliding history window (last 10 readings) and recognizes negative physiological trends like Rising Heart Rate or Falling SpO2. Sends Predictive Alerts before values hit emergency levels.
4. Smart Companion Features
SOS Button: Instantly triggers an emergency siren and broadcasts an urgent Telegram message with the patient's exact location.
Medication Reminders: Sound-based and Telegram reminders trigger every 4 hours to keep the patient on schedule.
Periodic Health Summary: Every 5 minutes (configurable), SAATHI compiles average, minimum, and maximum readings and messages a summary report to the caregiver.
WiFi Watchdog & Queue: Continually monitors WiFi connectivity. If WiFi drops during an emergency, it queues the pending Telegram alert and dispatches it immediately upon reconnection.
🔌 Hardware Setup & Pin Mapping
The system operates on an I2C bus and standard analog/digital GPIOs.

Connection Table
Component	Pin on ESP32	Description
ESP32 DevKit V1	-	Main Microcontroller
MAX30102 (SpO2)	SDA (GPIO 21), SCL (GPIO 22)	Heart Rate & Pulse Oximeter Sensor
MPU6050	SDA (GPIO 21), SCL (GPIO 22)	3-Axis Accelerometer & Gyroscope
I2C LCD (16x2)	SDA (GPIO 21), SCL (GPIO 22)	Character display for system states & vitals
Active Buzzer	GPIO 25	Audio siren, warnings, and alerts
LM35 Sensor	GPIO 34	Analog Temperature Sensor
SOS / Cancel Button	GPIO 14	Push Button (Pulled HIGH, active LOW)
