🚀 Setup & Installation
1. Prerequisites & Libraries
Ensure you have the Arduino IDE (or VSCode + PlatformIO) set up with ESP32 board support. Install the following libraries through the Library Manager:

Wire.h (Built-in)
LiquidCrystal_I2C by Frank de Brabander
SparkFun MAX3010x Pulse and Proximity Sensor Library by SparkFun Electronics
WiFi.h, HTTPClient.h, WiFiClientSecure.h (ESP32 Core Built-ins)
2. Network & Cloud Credentials
Open the source code file and configure the credentials for your environment:

WiFi Configuration
cpp

const char* ssid     = "YOUR_WIFI_SSID";
const char* password = "YOUR_WIFI_PASSWORD";
Telegram Bot Setup
Chat with @BotFather on Telegram to create a bot and retrieve your BOT_TOKEN.
Retrieve your Telegram account's numeric chat ID using @userinfobot or a similar bot and configure:
cpp

const String BOT_TOKEN = "YOUR_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN";
const String CHAT_ID   = "YOUR_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID";
JSONBin Configuration (Web Dashboard Integration)
Register on JSONBin.io.
Create a new private/public bin containing a template JSON matching SAATHI's structure.
Retrieve your API Master Key and Bin ID:
cpp

const String BIN_ID  = "YOUR_BIN_ID";
const String BIN_KEY = "$2a$10$YOUR_MASTER_KEY";
Location Coordinates (Mock/Static GPS)
Configure the hardcoded patient coordinates (or substitute with an active GPS library like TinyGPS++ if integrating a Neo-6M module):

cpp


const String HARD_MAPS_LINK = "https://maps.app.goo.gl/sVwVgf5MxSxPY9t59";
🔍 Code Walkthrough & Control Logic
Non-Blocking Sampling: Vitals collection takes place in a loop that checks for falls and button-presses during each individual sample cycle. This ensures that fall detection is highly responsive, even while calculating complex heart rates.
Fall Detection Verification State:
cpp

if (mag < FREEFALL_THRESHOLD) {
    // Free fall detected, now monitor for impact
    if (impact_detected_within_window) {
        // Enter 10-second countdown state
        // Poll Cancel Button
        // Send Telegram Alert if not cancelled
    }
}
Abnormality Filters:
cpp

if (heartRate > 120) highBpmCount++; else highBpmCount = 0;
if (highBpmCount >= 3) {
    // Trigger Siren & Telegram Alert
}
📈 JSONBin Data Schema
When updating the web dashboard, SAATHI performs an HTTP PUT request with the following JSON structure:

json

{
  "bpm": 76,
  "spo2": 98,
  "temperature": 36.8,
  "fall": false,
  "sos": false,
  "battery": 100,
  "latitude": 22.990508,
  "longitude": 88.454008,
  "healthScore": 100,
  "status": "Normal",
  "trend": "Stable",
  "bpmHistory": [75, 74, 76, 75, 76],
  "spo2History": [98, 97, 98, 98, 98],
  "tempHistory": [36.7, 36.7, 36.8, 36.8, 36.8]
}
